        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6766b6d7-2330-550b-a679-49561e890bd9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thornton Wilder, Richard Llewellyn, Huw Morgan\n- Works: The Long Christmas Dinner, How Green Was My Valley\n- Roles: playwright, novelist, narrator, main character\n- Places: Wales\n- Topics: Welsh family, mining community\n\nFacts:\n- Thornton Wilder was born on April 17, 1897, and was an American playwright and novelist.\n- Richard Llewellyn was born as Richard Dafydd Vivian Llewellyn Lloyd on December 8, 1906, and was a British novelist who used the pen name Richard Llewellyn.\n- Thornton Wilder wrote the one-act play The Long Christmas Dinner in 1931.\n- Richard Llewellyn published the novel How Green Was My Valley in 1939.\n- How Green Was My Valley is narrated by Huw Morgan, the main character, and is about his Welsh family and the mining community in which they live.\n- Thornton Wilder died on December 7, 1975.\n- Richard Llewellyn died on November 30, 1983.",
